PARSFILE
#FullDataName Models: Simulink`Base Model`
#RunMdlFile Extensions\Simulink\Base_Model.mdl
#RingCtrl1 2
OPT_INT_METHOD 2
#CheckBox0 0    
*USE_ALT_DIR 0
#CheckBox1 0    
*USE_DIFF_SOLVERS 0
#CheckBox2 0    
OPT_IO_UPDATE 0
#CheckBox3 0    

#MiscYellow0
LIVE_SERVER localhost
#ENDMYellow

#BlueLink0 ` , Import` , Import` , Import`

LIVE_SERVER_UPDATE_FREQ_MAX 60

#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#This dataset uses a Simulink model with the CarSim S-Function2v (instead of CarSim S-Function or CarSim S-Function2), to show how live video can be enabled.
#
#Besides using the video S-Function, it is also necessary to use the command "LIVE_SERVER localhost" to enable live communication between the VS Solver and VS Visualizer.
#
#This Simulink example does not add any features to the math model. It contains only two blocks: S-Function2v and Time.
#
#
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

